        "title": "feat(durable): add durable session task runtime foundation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis PR adds the opt-in, local-first durable runtime foundation proposed by PR1. The target failure mode is coordinator silence: long-running session/task/subagent work can continue across many steps, branches, and process restarts, but operators and runtime code need a bounded durable projection of which run, step, child, signal, or recovery state is open.\n\nThis is not a general-purpose workflow engine and does not include Work module, Workboard UI/tools, Task Flow projection adapters, or product-specific logic.\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nThis is PR2 in the replacement durable runtime stack:\n\n1. PR1: durable session/task runtime RFC v2.\n2. PR2: durable runtime foundation, this PR.\n3. PR3: agent/session/subagent wiring on top of this foundation.\n\nThis PR is designed to be reviewable independently as a core foundation slice.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds:\n\n- `durable_runtime_*` tables in the shared OpenClaw state DB;\n- SQLite store lifecycle with schema version checks and shared state permission hardening;\n- runtime runs, steps, events, refs, links, timers, and signals;\n- local-first claim/release, heartbeat, recovery, and bounded worker helpers;\n- read-only CLI and Gateway inspection surfaces;\n- generic coordination projection with unsupported write controls disabled;\n- Kysely generated types and guardrails for the new schema.\n\n## Explicit Non-Scope\n\n- Work module behavior.\n- Workboard UI/tools.\n- Task Flow projection adapters.\n- Retention/compaction policy.\n- Postgres/multi-worker lease contention.\n- Automatic retry/resume policy.\n- Ledger-only write controls.\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused validation observed locally:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable`\n  - 14 files, 53 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts`\n  - 2 files, 4 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/state/openclaw-state-db.test.ts src/state/openclaw-agent-db.test.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts`\n  - 4 files, 47 tests passed, 2 skipped.\n- Exact durable matrix requested on the older durable-core PR:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts src/durable/coordination-projection.test.ts src/durable/fan-in.test.ts src/durable/executor.test.ts src/durable/subagent.test.ts`\n  - 6 files, 36 tests passed.\n- Shared-state permission/query-plan matrix:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/state/openclaw-state-db.test.ts src/state/openclaw-state-db.permissions.test.ts src/state/sqlite-query-plan.test.ts`\n  - 3 files, 26 tests passed, 1 skipped.\n- `node scripts/generate-kysely-types.mjs --verify` passed.\n- `node scripts/check-kysely-guardrails.mjs` passed with `Kysely guardrails OK`.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check --threads=1 <changed durable/state/gateway files>` passed on 47 files.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n\nFull stack typecheck proof is recorded on PR3, which includes this PR2 foundation plus agent/session wiring.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR replaces the foundation portion of #97508 with smaller runtime-oriented naming and a narrower review boundary.\n",
